# What NOT to upload to EAS Build.
#
# This file lives at the REPO root, not in react-native-app, because that is
# where the archive is rooted. eas.json sits in react-native-app, but the
# project is inside this git repo and EAS archives from the repo, so the
# Laravel side rides along: `nativephp` alone is 607 MB and is neither tracked
# nor gitignored, which is exactly the combination EAS includes.
#
# The 1.0.58 builds each uploaded 1000 MB and spent over five minutes doing it.
#
# IMPORTANT: where EAS honours this file it uses it INSTEAD OF .gitignore, not
# in addition to it. Anything heavy has to be named here even when .gitignore
# already covers it - which is why vendor, dist and node_modules are repeated.

# --- Laravel side: none of it is used to build the Android app -------------
nativephp/
dist/
vendor/
node_modules/
storage/framework/
storage/logs/
bootstrap/cache/
public/build/
public/storage/
database/*.sqlite

# --- React Native app ------------------------------------------------------
react-native-app/node_modules/
react-native-app/android/build/
react-native-app/android/app/build/
react-native-app/android/app/.cxx/
react-native-app/android/.gradle/
react-native-app/android/.kotlin/
react-native-app/android/local.properties
react-native-app/ios/build/
react-native-app/ios/Pods/
react-native-app/.expo/
react-native-app/web-build/

# --- Build artifacts and noise ---------------------------------------------
*.apk
*.aab
*.hprof
*.log
coverage/
.git/
.github/
.idea/
.vscode/
.DS_Store

# NOT excluded on purpose: react-native-app/credentials.json and the keystore
# under react-native-app/android/app/. The production profile signs with
# credentialsSource: local, and signing must not break to save a few KB.
